Add --stream-size=# option

Certain streaming situations can result in significantly different compression ratios between a file and stdin (streaming the same file). This is mainly an issue for smaller source sizes, where the default compression parameters are not appropriate.

This diff adds a `--stream-size` option, which allows the user to specify the exact size of the incoming stream. Note that this specified size _must_ be the exact size of the stream, or else zstd will fail with `error 11`.

Tests have been added for comparing the compression ratio of a small file and streaming that small file, requiring that the difference is less than 0.05%.

Resolves #1720.

