Use safepaths for run download

## Description

Fixes #10007 

### Implementation

As described in https://github.com/cli/cli/issues/10007#issuecomment-2517653620, the issue at hand is that when a specific artifact is targeted, `gh` will unpack it in the directory specified by `--dir`. If unspecified, it defaults to the current dir `.`. Therefore, we were checking whether `.` descended from `.` and determined that it did not, incorrectly reporting a file traversal.

In my opinion, it's **extremely** challenging to reason about all the combinations of relative paths that could be provided (just look at [these tests](https://github.com/cli/cli/compare/trunk...wm%2Fsafepaths?body=&expand=1&title=Use+safepaths+for+run+download#diff-6225ebdad7e6af5d2caa9dece1982922e07b07f960b23066f2ffec2cd4287093L27-L212). I think it's better for us to work with absolute paths where possible.

I've previously proposed canonicalization of paths (also resolving symlinks) but for the moment enforcing absolute paths seems sufficient. We rely on a new type `safepaths.Absolute` that can be joined with elements to create new absolute paths, or will error if the new path would result in a traversal.

### Testing

I added a new acceptance test that asserts correct traversal failure.

