Exit with 1 on authentication issues

Fixes #8845

If any user account entry is not a `validEntry` it returns a `SilentError`, so that the command exits with 1.

This also respects the filtering with `--hostname`.

> Given any (active or inactive) account has issues with authentication
When I run `gh auth status`
Then the exit code is **non-zero**
And all entries are printed to **stderr**
> 
> Given any (active or inactive) account on github.com has issues with authentication
When I run `gh auth status --hostname github.com`
Then the exit code is **non-zero**
And all entries are printed to **stderr**
> 
> Given any (active or inactive) account on github.com has issues with authentication
When I run `gh auth status --hostname ghe.io`
Then the exit code is **zero**
And all entries are printed to **stdout**

**To-Do:**

- [x] Update manual to include exit code behaviour

