Delete local branch more often when merging PR

The local branch now gets deleted even if the remote branch cannot be deleted (e.g. when the remote branch belongs to a fork) when using `gh pr merge -d`.

Fixes #7355

## Examples
**When a branch can be deleted locally and remotely**

Before:
```
✓ Merged pull request #10 (Blueberries are a good fruit)
✓ Deleted branch blueberries and switched to branch fruit
```

After:
```
✓ Merged pull request #10 (Blueberries are a good fruit)
✓ Deleted local branch blueberries and switched to branch fruit
✓ Deleted remote branch blueberries
```

**When a branch can be deleted locally but not remotely**

Before:
```
✓ Merged pull request #10 (Blueberries are a good fruit)
```

After:
```
✓ Merged pull request #10 (Blueberries are a good fruit)
✓ Deleted local branch blueberries and switched to branch main
```

## Notes

I have only tested the new behavior using the tests contained in `merge_test.go`, some manual testing before merging from the reviewers would be appreciated.

