Add `--pattern` field to `run download`

<!--
  Thank you for contributing to GitHub CLI!
  To reference an open issue, please write this in your description: `Fixes #NUMBER`
-->
Fixes #5166 

Adds `--pattern` field to `run download` allowing users to pass in glob patterns. It can be used with `--name`.

## Example:

### Download all .log artifacts
`gh run download 123456 -p *.log`

### Download all .md files and a specific json file
`gh run download 123456 -p *.md -n specific_name.json`

---

If both `--name` and `--pattern` match the same file name it will not be downloaded twice.

