Allow default host

This PR changes behavior to automatically determine a default host to use rather than always defaulting to dotcom. If there is one authenticated host that is used as the default. This PR includes the infrastructure so that in the near future the default host will be able to be set in the configuration file also. 

This PR is pretty large and it is HIGHLY recommended to be viewed through each commit individually. The reason it is so large is because we used to use `ghinstance.DefaultHost()` to determine the default host but to support this feature we need to use the config file to determine the default host. Much of the PR code is replacing instances of `ghinstance.DefaultHost()` with calls to the config file. Many of these replacements were easy copy paste changes that resulted in no functional changes. The one place this became a bit trickier was in the remote resolver where the logic needed to changed.

Additionally the first commit is a restructuring commit that extracts config code into separate files, with no functional changes, to make it easier to understand. Now `config_type.go` is the `config` interface definition and `from_env.go` and `from_file.go` are implementations of the `config` interface, and `config_map.go` is the underlying data structure for a `config`.

closes #1745

