Fix the error logic and error message for suggesting `--` before a flag

Closes #1284 BurntSushi/ripgrep#936
Related: #1744 #1943
The features disgussed in this issue was already implemented. However the error message emission introduced by #1514 is misleading.

The word `PATTERN` in the current error message comes from ripgrep-specific usage information, which is misleading in other applications. 

The error message should only be emitted when the argument looks like a flag(which is the only way the argument can be processed counterintuitively). 

This is also the first step on solving #1744 #1943.

