Don't raise error if external program failed in the middle of pipeline

# Description
Tried to make a quick fix on #13868 

This pr introduce a new config value called `display_error::exit_code_on_pipeline_element`, but it's only useful while creating a `ByteStream::child`, and the value is un-configuble in `config.nu` now.

I think it maybe useful when we want to check the child executing result on pipeline elements, so it's also relative to #13817.

@IanManske I'm not sure if it's a proper way to change, feel free to close it if you don't agree with the idea.

# User-Facing Changes
Fixes #13868 , than I hope most internal commands doesn't show errors if previous pipeline command runs into failed.

# Tests + Formatting
Added 1 test.


