[Material][Popover] Add support for virtual element as anchorEl

<!-- Thanks so much for your PR, your contribution is appreciated! ❤️ -->

- [x] I have followed (at least) the [PR section of the contributing guide](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/HEAD/CONTRIBUTING.md#sending-a-pull-request).

### Changes

Add documentation, demo, and tests for using a virtual element (VE) as an anchor element for the `Popover` component.

- This doesn't require changes in the component, only to update the type and proptype for the `anchorEl` prop. Fixed previous definition: when providing a function for the anchor, the [function doesn't receive any arguments](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/master/packages/mui-material/src/Popover/Popover.js#L62).
- The virtual element is different from the one used for [`Popper`](https://mui.com/material-ui/react-popper/#virtual-element) and [`Tooltip`](https://mui.com/material-ui/react-tooltip/#virtual-element), as the `Popover` [expects the VE's `nodeType` property to be `1`](https://github.com/mui/material-ui/blob/master/packages/mui-material/src/Popover/Popover.js#L169) (which is the type for [`Node.ELEMENT_NODE`](https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/API/Node/nodeType)).

### Screenshot of the new VE section on the docs

<img width="1227" alt="Screenshot of the new VE section" src="https://github.com/mui/material-ui/assets/16889233/73a695cd-54e6-437b-ad93-08a7b8f0bb54">

Closes #36416



