[base] Add `ClassNameProvider` to support custom className in multiple scopes

<!-- Thanks so much for your PR, your contribution is appreciated! ❤️ -->

close #29856

**Summary**
The current approach of https://mui.com/guides/classname-generator/#main-content does not support multiple scopes in an application which is considered as regression because it was possible in v4.

This PR introduces a react context that can control generated className of any components in `material`, `joy` or `base`  with multiple scopes support. Here is what it looks like:

```js
import { experimental_ClassNameProvider } from '@mui/material/utils';
import Button from '@mui/material/Button';

const generateFooClassName = (componentName) => componentName.replace('Mui', 'Foo');
const generateBarClassName = (componentName) => componentName.replace('Mui', 'Bar');

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <ClassNameProvider generateClassName={generateFooClassName}>
        <Button>Foo</Button> // FooButton-root
      </ClassNameProvider>
      <ClassNameProvider generateClassName={generateBarClassName}>
        <Button>Bar</Button> // BarButton-root
      </ClassNameProvider>
    </div>
  )
}
```

> The prop name is the same as `StylesProvider` API in v4 https://mui.com/styles/api/#stylesprovider

Open as a draft to get early feedback on the names and the implementation before I update the entire codebase follow the checklist below. Please review [by commit](https://github.com/mui-org/material-ui/pull/29901/commits).

